# MadGraph5 batch script: g g > g g at LO (QCD).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - Four external gluons exercise the 4-gluon vertex, the only SM vertex with
#     k > 1 color structures (expanded x3 per color-index chain), and pure-f
#     color algebra. full_simplify reduces every f-product to the 6-element
#     single-trace basis, giving NCOLOR=6 with the standard SU(3) four-gluon
#     color matrix (diagonal 19/6, reverse-pair 2/3, else -1/3).
#   - The stress test for the per-chain rooting of multi-structure vertices and
#     the largest CF contraction in the SM tree-level vocabulary.
#   - One concrete subprocess => the matrix element is matrix1 (no matrix9).
#
# MadEvent output (default): `launch` builds matrix1_optim.f for the timing
# comparison and integrates the partonic cross section. lpp=0 => fixed-energy
# partonic gluon beams, so the result is the partonic sigma-hat.
generate g g > g g
output gg_to_gg -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
